Z||000010||Fierochic88||09-25-2001||07:42 PM||||Man sorry to hear about that.  Joe's (FieroGT914) 86GT got hit yesteday too.  He has probably about $800 in damage and that is just a rough estimate from the body shop.  I hope your car gets better soon!<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroGT 914||09-25-2001||08:22 PM||||Hey Voytek... I feel for ya bud - yesterday I was on my way back from picking up a set of GT tail lights from the post office up here at school and I was sitting in traffic.  Some dude in a jeep cherokee coasted foward behind me and he forgot to use his brakes - crack! right into the back of my 86 GT and just the estimate without inspecting for structural damage was almost $800 like jen said.  really sucks but what can ya do?:-\<P>------------------<BR>Joe<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/j/j/jjr161/FieroGT914_Signature.gif">         <BR>AOL I.M.: FieroGT 914<BR>White 86 1/2 GT (Stock)<BR>Maroon 87 GT (Mod)<BR><A HREF="http://www.personal.psu.edu/~jjr161" TARGET=_blank>My Website</A>||||reg||9
Z||000012||fropuff||09-25-2001||11:42 PM||||Very sorry to hear that.  At least that it's certainly not your fault.  In my case, it's my word against the other guys.  My story is at: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010441.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010441.html</A> <P>Some before and after pics are at: <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1781133&a=13779742&f=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1781133&a=13779742&f=0</A>  <P>Damages totaled $2783.10, and I have no idea if I'll be paying it or not.  Good luck!  Hope tomorrow is better for ya!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||09-25-2001||11:56 PM||||Hey man, sorry to hear about your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <BR>Feels like our children getting hurt.<P>The ajuster knows what she speaks of, the Fiero can take a what looks externally like just a 'minor ding' in a rather major collision.<P>It's the plastic bumpers, they really bounce back (but underneeth there could be QUITE a bit of damage, possibly even to structual material)<P>Sorry to hear about it, some *******  rear-ended me (****er just took of from a red light, only with me infront of him. He was in a pickup with this nice ramming bar on the front.  claims he 'didn't see me' I calimed he owed me $2k for repairs (he did) and got it.  <P>I mean, the cars are low, but come on!!  you don't see the car right infront of you that you've been following for more than two blocks?!<P>people suck. <P>That's my rant for today, I feel better now!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>I'll just whine for a moment and then I'll shut up.<P>I was on my way to work.  At 7:59 AM, about 3 blocks away from where I work (I was going to be on time for once), the traffic came to a stop - someone was turning.  So I look in the rear view mirror and there is this GrandAm that I raced (and beat) on the highway 2 minutes earlier.  He did look like he was catching up pretty fast.  2 seconds later - wham!  'MY BABY IS HURT' I thought (actually, I swore).<P>When all was said and done, I ended up with about $1200 worth of damage (according to the adjustor).<P>AND, get this: the insurance claim person (lady) says this: 'Oh, it's a Fiero? Then you better file a police report - it'll most likely have quite a bit of damage'.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> ?????!!!!!  Yeah, OK.  The GrandAm actually looked worse.<P>Just had to share my story.<BR>I think it's time for a whole new paint job.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000014||Brandon86SE||09-26-2001||12:18 AM||||grr....<P>Wish I woulda been there, I would've kicked his ass (not that you would've needed my help, I'm sure he felt beaten up by the look he would've got)!  At least it was only $1800, much more than that and it would've been over book value.  And it had to happen 5 days before the Red Deer run!  Gonna take the coupe then?  Hope she's better soon, and a new paint job is really in order now!  Cya,<P>Brandon <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000015||Smoooooth GT||09-26-2001||07:52 AM||||voytech...  I'm sorry to hear about your car...   I got T-boned and hit from the front in my 87GT, It was a total mess (1987Chevy Dually T-boned me in passengerside door..  and a new Cavalier hit me head on from thew front) I got a check for $4,800.00 and I paid them $100.00 and they gave me the GT back..   I used the motor, fascia GT clip all for the Smooooth GT Conversion...  So IF  you can get it back...  do it...   Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4.JPG"> ||||reg||1
